Z||000000||DR650SE||11-01-2001||11:53 AM||||Is this side scoop worth my money and time to paint and put on?  Will it help and if so how much?  Do you suggest I drop that dime?  Let me know if you like it if you got it. Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||1
Z||000001||falconhulk||11-01-2001||12:01 PM||||what scoop would that be??||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||11-01-2001||02:15 PM||||I had a holley scoop for a while and now I have the panel scoops. The only advantage the scoops provide is a positive cool air pressure in the intake system. From a "performance" stand point you may see a .5-1 horsepower increase but only at highway speeds. All they do is provide a better throttle response when going down the highway. There is even an increase in fuel ecomomy of maybe a mile per gallon. The advantages are very minor. It won't change you 0-60 or 1/4 mile times. I bought the panels for appearence and to aid in cooling the engine compartment. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rick 88||11-01-2001||07:12 PM||||Hey, side scoops are worth at least 50 hp. in the "looks" dept. 25 hp. per side!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Pontiac should have done this from the factory along with a nice hood vent.<P>Rick 88||||reg||12
Z||000004||grinthock||11-01-2001||07:25 PM||||When I tested my holly scoop with a scantool.<P>On the SAME identical night with less than 3mph/wind.  I drove a 2 klm route. <P>I saw a 5% gain in MAP voltage on the second run, both runs were done at the same RPM during data collection while the engine was the same temp.<P>What all that means?  HEll I dunno, it means it did SOMETHING.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroworld.com</A>  The place to go for Fiero INFO! <BR>Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DR650SE||11-01-2001||10:18 PM||||Thanks, at least something happens<P>------------------<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||6
Z||000006||revin||11-02-2001||10:04 AM||||Check with Doug Kinney at fierowarehouse(dmkfiero@ovis.net). he has the killer scoops! Very easy to install and the looks are out of this world!! I think the $150 I paid for them was too cheap. You get the whole panel, just rivit them in! (hint: pep boys[auto store] have large washer rivits that work very well.<BR>I can tell more power is there.It sounds like someone took off the air cleaner off a carb. Did I say how cool they look?||||reg||14
